    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>A supplement asks the insurer to revise its estimate on an open claim to add missed items, correct quantities or pricing, or include damage found after the first inspection.</li>
<li>Commonly missed hail items include starter, drip edge, ridge cap, flashing, roof vents, gutters, window screens, rooftop HVAC components, and steep or high-roof labor.</li>
<li>Hidden damage, such as deteriorated or damaged decking or extra shingle layers, often appears only during tear-off and needs prompt photos and notice.</li>
